  "reason": "The RNA-only PCA baseline (config_001) achieved only 0.485 accuracy, which is very low and could reflect either an uninformative RNA representation or a fundamentally difficult task. The most critical uncertainty at this stage is whether the image modality carries stronger predictive signal than RNA. Testing config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the modality question while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) and model complexity comparable to the RNA baseline. If image accuracy substantially exceeds 0.485, it directs remaining budget toward image-centric or multimodal configurations; if it is similarly low, it suggests the task is inherently hard and we should focus on learned encoders and aggregation strategies. This single comparison maximally reduces uncertainty about which modality to prioritize before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile designs."
}

